==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|hon|hōn}}, from {{inh|sv|non|hón}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*hēnō}}. Cognate with {{cog|is|hún}}, {{cog|da|hun}} and {{cog|nb|hun}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hʊn/|lang=sv}}
* {{audio|Sv-hon.ogg|audio|lang=sv}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|sv|pronoun}}

# [[she]]
#: {{ux|sv|'''Hon''' är mycket vacker.|t='''She''' is very beautiful.}}
# the [[time]], the [[car]], or the [[boat]], [[human]]
#: ''Vad är '''hon'''?''
#:: What's '''the time'''?
#: ''Går '''hon''' bra?''
#:: Is '''she''' (''the car'') working all right?

===Reason===
The reason that these nouns are referred to as "she" is that they were of feminine gender in old Swedish noun classification.

